course: dictionary
lesson: 2656
title: Devastate: destroy and shock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Devastate is a strong word. It means to destroy a place so badly that little is left, or to hurt someone so deeply that they feel shattered. When a word is this strong, look at the words around it to see which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The An Lushan rebellion, 755 to 763, devastated the Tang» is about a place. A war badly damaged a whole country, and the number of people counted fell sharply. Here devastated means badly damaged. Test it: swap in "badly damaged" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Now look at a feeling: «She was devastated by the news.» No building was wrecked here. The clue is the news, and the person was deeply shocked and sad. Whether the text is about places or people tells you which meaning to choose.
explain: Watch the forms. Devastated describes how someone feels, as in «left devastated». Devastating describes the thing that causes the feeling, as in «a devastating fire». Informally, «a devastating goal» means an amazing goal.
fact: Devastate is a verb: you can devastate, devastates, devastated or devastating.
fact: «Devastate» means to destroy or badly damage a place, so that little is left.
fact: «Devastate» can also mean to make someone feel terribly shocked and sad.
fact: «Devastating» can mean extremely strong or impressive, as in «a devastating goal».
fact: In history, the An Lushan rebellion of 755 to 763 devastated the Tang dynasty in China.
exercise: «The flood devastated the farms along the river.» What does devastated mean here? | *Badly damaged, so little is left | Made into a lake for boats | Gently watered | Painted bright green
exercise: «She was devastated when her dog ran away.» What does devastated mean here? | Extremely tired from running | Very hungry | Excited about a trip | *Terribly shocked and sad
exercise: «He scored a devastating goal in the last minute.» What does devastating suggest? | Sad and terrible | *Extremely strong or impressive | Made of wood | Very quiet
test: «The town was devastated by the storm.» What does devastated mean? | Very warm and sunny | *Badly damaged, with much destroyed | Full of visitors | Newly painted
test: Grandma says, «The news left me devastated.» What does devastated show about her? | Very hungry for lunch | Happy to hear the news | Bored and sleepy | *Deeply shocked and sad
exam: Which sentence uses devastating to mean extremely impressive? | «He felt devastated after the lost match» | «The devastated village was rebuilt slowly» | *«Her devastating goal won the match in the final minute» | «The devastating storm knocked down power lines»
